\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 1) \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 From Mars With Love}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Villain: Baron Blade
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Environment: Wagner Mars Base
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Required Heroes: Legacy
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 The set-up:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Dr. Julius Wagner, famed astronaut and xeno-geologist, has approached his good friend L\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
egacy with a problem.  All communication with the Wagner Mars Base (named after Dr. Wagner) has been cut off.  The base\hich\f1 \rquote \loch\f1 
s final communication suggested that perhaps the base was under attack by unknown forces.  Legacy and the heroes agree to fly Dr. Wagne\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 r\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  to Mars in their rocket plane to investigate.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Once they arrive at the base, the heroes discover that Baron Blade has taken it over, and plans on using his TerraLunar Impulsion Beam to drag the Earth\hich\f1 \rquote \loch\f1 
s moon into the Earth unless the heroes can stop him.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Win condition:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 1) The heroes must defeat Baron Blade
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 2) Dr. Wagner must not die.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Dr. Wagner has 10 hp and is considered a hero target, so that any card, power, or ability that affects all heroes or all hero targets will affect Dr. Wagner as well.  However\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
, anytime Dr. Wagner would take damage, any hero may choose to redirect the damage themselves instead.  As with all redirected damage, the source and type of the damage remains the same, and the hero may further redirect or reduce the damage again with po
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 w\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 ers or abilities as usual.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 2) \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Ancient Programming}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Villain: Omnitron
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Environment: Ruins of Atlantis
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Required Heroes: Ra
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 The set-up:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Ra has managed to uncover the location of the Lost Runestones of Atlantis, ancient tablets that supposedly contain\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
 mystical codes of great power.  Gathering a group of heroes, Ra begins an excursion to retrieve them.  But upon reaching the sunken city, they discover that Omnitron is also searching for the artifacts and that the giant robot plans to incorporate the an
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 c\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 ient code into its programming to greatly increase its power.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Can the heroes retrieve the artifacts before Omnitron can incorporate their code?
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Win condition:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 1) The heroes must defeat Omnitron.
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 2) The heroes must find all of the artifacts.  There are (H x 3) artifacts.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 \hich\f1 Heroes find an artifact by \'93\loch\f1 \hich\f1 burning\'94\loch\f1 \hich\f1  a card; any time a hero could play a card in the usual fashion, they may \'93\loch\f1 \hich\f1 burn\'94\loch\f1 
 it instead by playing it face-down and not applying its effect\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
s.  All rules that affect playing cards affect burning cards, meaning that if an effect in play prevents the card from being played, then it cannot be burned either.  But the burned card is not actually put into play, and none of the text on the card is e
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 v\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 er taken into account in the game.  Burned cards do not go into the trash as usual, but are set aside.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 3) \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 The Coronal Codex}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Villain: Citizen Dawn
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Environment: Insula Primalis
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Required Heroes: Visionary, Haka
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 The set-up:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 While meditating, Visiona\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
ry has a startling precognitive vision of a large glowing cube covered in unreadable symbols.  This is the Coronal Codex, a device which was stranded on Earth when an alien spaceship crash landed.  Most troubling of all, the vision showed that Citizen Daw
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 n\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  and her group of super-powered followers are on their way to the crash site to break into the spaceship to gain control of the Codex.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Visionary and the heroes must make their way to Insula Primalis and retrieve the Coronal Codex from the crashed spaceshi\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 p before Citizen Dawn and her followers can.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Win condition:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 1) The heroes must defeat Citizen Dawn.
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 2) The heroes must break all three layers of protective crystalline matrices that protect the Coronal Codex to retrieve it.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 The Coronal Codes is protected\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  by three interlocking crystalline matrices, each of which must be circumvented to get to the next matrix.  To circumvent the first matrix, the heroes must do (H) 
}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 different }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
types of damage to any target or combination of villain or environment targets acro\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 ss any period of time.  The same hero doesn\hich\f1 \rquote \loch\f1 
t need to do all of them (although if one hero does do them all, that counts), and the instances of damage may be spread out in time in any way.  At least one point of the damage must be done for it to count for\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 that damage type.  Multiple instances of the same kind of damage are irrelevant.  Damage that has its type converted uses the final converted type, not what it started out as.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 For example, in a three-hero game, Hero A does one point of fire damage to a Ci\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
tizen, then a few rounds goes by with no one else doing any damage.  Then Hero B does 5 points of fire damage to another Citizen, which doesn\hich\f1 \rquote \loch\f1 
t help since fire damage has already been done.  Next, Hero C does 2 points of psychic damage to an environment c\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 a\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
rd which is converted into toxic damage, so at this point, two of the three locks on the first matrix have been broken by fire and toxic damage.  Lastly, Hero A does 1 point of projectile damage to multiple targets, including Dawn herself.  The number of 
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 t\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 argets doesn\hich\f1 \rquote \loch\f1 t matter, but the fact that this is a third kind of damage means that the first Matrix has been circumvented.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 To circumvent the second matrix, everything is reset and the heroes must now do a total of (H + 1) different types of damage, irresp\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
ective of what kinds of damage were done to the first matrix.  So for example, if fire damage was done to the first matrix, it can be done again to the second matrix (once) to count as one of the types of damage.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 To circumvent the third matrix, everything\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
 is reset again and the heroes must now do a total of (H + 2) different types of damage, irrespective of what kinds of damage were done to the previous two matrices.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 4) The Wedding of the Century}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Villain: Grand Warlord Voss
