\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 1) The heroes mus\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 t defeat Baron Blade before the power transfer is complete (i.e. before the villain trash contains 15 cards).
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Instead of the moon crashing into the Earth when Baron Blade\hich\f1 \rquote \loch\f1 s villain trash contains 15 cards, his transfer of power from Legacy to himself is c\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
omplete when 15 cards are in his villain trash.  The heroes must defeat Baron Blade before this happens.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 As more cards accumulate in the villain trash, more of Young Legacy\hich\f1 \rquote \loch\f1 s power has been transferred to Baron Blade.  Add these conditions to Baron Blade\hich\f1 \rquote \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
s villain card:
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - At the start of the villain turn, if the villain trash has 5 or more cards in it, damage dealt to villains, minions and devices is reduced by 1.
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - At the start of the villain turn, if the villain trash has 10 or more cards in it, damag\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 e dealt by villains, minions, and devices is increased by 1.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 The first condition will still be true when the second condition is met, so by the time there are 10 cards in the villain trash, both the damage reduction and bonus damage effects will be in play.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 11) Red Planet Shootout}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Villain: Citizen Dawn
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Enviro\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 nment: Wagner Mars Base
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Required Heroes: Bunker, Ra, Tempest, [Expatriette]
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 The set-up:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Sitting around the Sentinel\hich\f1 \rquote \loch\f1 s HQ, the heroes get into a friendly argument over who is the team's best blaster.  Bunker, Ra, and Tempest (and Expatriette, if you're \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
playing with her) each think they are the best in the group and each has their favorite story of how they took down a villain or goon at just the right moment to save the day.  But of course, no one has any way to actually prove who is the best.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 And then \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
they receive the call.  Citizen Dawn has taken over the Wagner Mars Base and has declared it to be the homeland for a new nation populated by her superpowered followers.  Excited at the prospect of settling their argument once and for all, the heroes race
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 to their rocket plane, declaring that this shootout on the Red Planet will finally show who is truly the best.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Win condition:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 1) The heroes must defeat Citizen Dawn.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 There are no other win conditions for this scenario beyond simply defeating the villian.\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 \hich\f1 
  However, each of the heroes is also participating in a contest to see who can rack up the most \'93\loch\f1 \hich\f1 points\'94.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 A hero gets a point for every minion to which they deal the killing blow (i.e. their damage is responsible for sending the minion card to the villai\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
n trash).  Damage done to a minion that does not result in that minion being sent to the villain trash doesn\hich\f1 \rquote \loch\f1 
t score the hero a point.  The point is awarded to the hero who is doing the damage regardless of any boosts or help they receive for the attack f\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 r\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
om other heroes.  For example, if Tempest deals 1 damage, which is boosted by 1 by Legacy, which makes it enough to send a minion to the trash, Tempest receives one point and Legacy receives none for the attack.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 In addition to the points scored by taking \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 out minions, whichever hero deals the final bit of damage to Citizen Dawn herself receives 5 points.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 12) Big Game Hunter}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Villain: Grand Warlord Voss
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Environment: Insula Primalis
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Required Heroes: Haka, Tachyon, Absolute Zero
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 The set-up:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Haka's lo\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
ve affair with the wilds of Insula Primalis continues.  He wants to go back to the secluded area to hunt the jungle's great reptiles for sport.  Tachyon is horrified at this idea, saying that the reptiles should be studied, not hunted.  Absolute Zero prop
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 o\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
ses a compromise in which Tachyon gathers samples from the beasts while Haka is attempting to best the creatures in combat.  This is deemed acceptable to all, and the heroes head off to Insula Primalis.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
Not surprisingly, things get more complicated when, while hunting the elusive reptiles, the heroes come upon Grand Warlord Voss and his invasion vanguard.  Neither Haka nor Tachyon are willing to give up their plans however, so while fighting Voss and his
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 minions, the hunt continues. 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Win condition:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 1) The heroes must defeat Grand Warlord Voss.
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 2) Three different reptiles must be defeated by Haka and sampled by Tachyon.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 To win this scenario, both of the following two conditions must be met (in addition to\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  defeating the villain as usual):
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 1) Haka must land the killing blow on three separate reptiles environment cards (Enraged T-Rex, Pterodactyl Thief, Velociraptor Attack).  The three need not be all different, so all three velociraptors, or two velocirapto
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
rs and a t-rex, etc. are acceptable.  If anyone besides Haka deals the damage to the environment card which sends it to the trash, then it does not count towards the total.  Haka does not need to do all the damage dealt to an environment card for it to co
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 u\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 nt, just the final bit of damage that sends it to the trash.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 2) Tachyon must deal any amount of damage to three separate reptile environment cards (Enraged T-Rex, Pterodactyl Thief, Velociraptor Attack), but must not do enough damage to send the card to t
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 he trash.  Doing damage to the same environment card multiple times (i.e. doing damage across subsequent rounds) isn't relevant, just the number of cards which are "sampled" by Tachyon.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 13) Girl's Night Out}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Villain: Baron Blade
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Environment: Megalopo\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 lis
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  - Required Heroes: Wraith, Fanatic, Visionary
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 The set-up:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Wraith must attend a big charity event in Megalopolis as her alter ego, and she manages to convince Fanatic and Visionary to accompany her for a girl's night out.  The event is a r\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
ousing success and everyone has a wonderful time meeting and partying with the rich, famous, and connected people of the city.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Unfortunately, just at the stroke of midnight, many of the famous figures at the party begin to shimmer and change as their appe\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
arances shift to become those of Baron Blade and his minions.  The Baron announces that he's hidden a bomb somewhere in the city which he will detonate unless he's paid an exorbitant ransom.  Quickly sneaking away to change costumes, the heroes reappear t
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 o\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
 confront Baron Blade, who calmly orders his minions to reassume their holographic disguises.  Laughing maniacally, the Baron asks how the heroes can possibly defeat him if they can't even tell friend from foe.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Win condition:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid5987008 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 1) The heroes must defeat Bar\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 on Blade before the bomb explodes (i.e. before the villain trash contains 15 cards).
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 The Baron\hich\f1 \rquote \loch\f1 s new super-tech allows him to holographically disguise anyone so that the heroes can\hich\f1 \rquote \loch\f1 t be certain if they\hich\f1 \rquote \loch\f1 
re attacking the bad guys, the good guys, or innocent\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  bystanders.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
Every time a hero deals damage to a villain card, roll a die.  On a roll of 2, the villain card being attacked has actually been disguised to look like one of the charity guests and that villain target is not a valid target for the hero until the beginnin
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 g\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
 of the hero's next turn.  The hero may choose a different villain target for the attack they are executing as long as more valid targets exist (which would require a new roll for each new target).  If there are no more valid targets available, the hero m
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 a\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 y not execute the attack.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
On a roll of 1, the hero has actually attacked one of their fellow heroes who has been holographically disguised to look like one of the minions.  In this case, the original attack is considered to have successfully landed on the
\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
 villain target, but the villain target is considered to be completely immune to the damage dealt.  In addition, the hero deals 1 point of damage of the same type as the original attack to the hero target with the highest hp other than themselves.
\par 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Only at\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 tacks on villain targets require a roll.  Attacks on environment targets do not require a roll.
